// GAME CUSTOMIZATION
////////////

#org @gText_GameCustomization_CustomizationPrompt
Welcome to Pok\emon Amethyst!\pDo you want to customize your\nexperience with the game?

#org @gText_GameCustomization_CustomizationMenu
Please choose which feature(s) you\nwould like to customize.

#org @gText_GameCustomization_Complete
Selections have been saved.\pSome settings can be changed in the\nOptions Menu's second page.\pWe hope you enjoy Pok\emon Amethyst!

#org @gText_GameCustomizationMenu_DifficultyMode
Difficulty Mode

#org @gText_GameCustomizationMenu_Tutorials
Tutorials

#org @gText_GameCustomizationMenu_StarterSelection
Starter Selection

#org @gText_GameCustomizationMenu_LevelCaps
Level Caps

#org @gText_GameCustomizationMenu_StartWithQoLItems
QoL Items

#org @gText_GameCustomizationMenu_SkipCutscenes
Skip Cutscenes

#org @gText_GameCustomizationMenu_Done
Done

#org @gText_GameCustomization_DifficultyMode_Prompt
The difficulty mode dictates how the\ngame is structured.\pStandard mode is the default and\nintended experience.\pHard mode gives all boss trainers\nstronger Pok\emon and held items.\pExtra Hard additionally gives each\ntrainer Pok\emon maxed IVs in all\lstats and maxed EVs in their\lhighest 2 stats.\pThis option can be changed later in\nthe Options Menu's second page.\pPlease select a mode.

#org @gText_GameCustomization_DifficultyModeOption_Standard
Standard Mode

#org @gText_GameCustomization_DifficultyModeOption_Hard
Hard Mode

#org @gText_GameCustomization_DifficultyModeOption_ExtraHard
Extra Hard Mode

#org @gText_GameCustomization_DifficultyMode_StandardSet
Standard Mode is enabled!

#org @gText_GameCustomization_DifficultyMode_HardSet
Hard Mode is enabled!

#org @gText_GameCustomization_DifficultyMode_ExtraHardSet
Extra Hard Mode is enabled!

#org @gText_GameCustomization_TutorializationQuestion
Would you like to enable early game\nbattling and catching tutorials?

#org @gText_GameCustomization_TutorializationTurnedOn
Tutorialization is enabled!

#org @gText_GameCustomization_TutorializationTurnedOff
Tutorialization is disabled!

#org @gText_GameCustomization_StarterGenerationPrompt
Choose which Pok\emon generation your\nStarter Pok\emon are from.\pYou may also set Shuffle mode to\nrandomly pick from gens 1-8.

#org @gText_GameCustomization_StarterGenerationSaved
Starter Generation choice saved!

#org @gText_GameCustomization_LevelCapsQuestion
You may choose to set soft or hard\nlevel caps.\pWhen soft caps are set, you may\nlevel your Pok\emon freely.\pThey will only obey your commands if\nyou have enough badges, however.\pThis is the intended experience for\nan initial playthrough.\pWhen hard caps are set, you will\nnot be able to level up past\lcertain thresholds, as determined\lby the next boss trainer.\pThis results in a more challenging\nexperience.\pThis option can be changed later in\nthe Options Menu's second page.\pWhich level capping do you prefer?

#org @gText_GameCustomization_LevelCapsOption_Soft
Soft (no restriction)

#org @gText_GameCustomization_LevelCapsOption_Hard
Hard (= next boss's ace)

#org @gText_GameCustomization_LevelCapsOption_ExtraHard
Extra Hard (-2 next boss's ace)

#org @gText_GameCustomization_SoftLevelCapsTurnedOn
Soft Level Caps are enabled!

#org @gText_GameCustomization_HardLevelCapsTurnedOn
Hard Level Caps are enabled!

#org @gText_GameCustomization_ExtraHardLevelCapsTurnedOn
Extra Hard Level Caps are enabled!

#org @gText_GameCustomization_QoLFromStart
This option gives QoL items like\nthe Exp. Share and Infinite Repel\lfrom the start of the game.\pThis option is recommended for\nplayers who wish to have a more\lrelaxing experience.\pThe items provided by this setting\nare normally found throughout the\lstory.\pDo you want to start the game\nwith all QoL items?

#org @gText_GameCustomization_QoLItemsOn
QoL items will be received when\nthe game starts!

#org @gText_GameCustomization_QoLItemsOff
QoL items will not be received when\nthe game starts!

#org @gText_GameCustomization_SkipCutscenesQuestion
This option allows you to replace\ncutscenes with short tips on where\lto go next.\pIt is only recommended for players in\nrepeat playthroughs, as skipped\lplot is not recapped.\pThis option can be changed later in\nthe Options Menu's second page.\pDo you want to skip cutscenes?

#org @gText_GameCustomization_SkipCutscenesTurnedOn
Cutscene skipping is enabled!

#org @gText_GameCustomization_SkipCutscenesTurnedOff
Cutscene skipping is disabled!

